# E-1025: Let $f$ be a function from all pairs of elements in $\{1,\ldots,n\}$ to $\{1,\ldots,n\}$ such that $f(x,y)\neq x$ and $\neq y$ for all $x,y$. We call $X\subseteq \{1,\ldots,n\}$ independent if whenever $x,y\in X$ we have $f(x,y)\not\in X$. Let $g(n)$ be such that, in every function $f$, there is an independent set of size at least $g(n)$. Estimate $g(n)$.
